; Tutorial_2_Install_and_Launch.inix -- installing HomerView and opening it.

[about]
Title=2 - Install and Launch
Intro=The installer finds your screen reader and sets up its scripts; then the key that opens HomerView from anywhere.
Setup=HomerView_setup.exe is downloaded from the HomerView page on GitHub.
Homework=Press Alt plus Shift plus H after installing and listen to the version line.

[step]

Say=One want: HomerView working with your screen reader, without a restart.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=I open the downloaded setup program and allow it to make changes.
Key=Enter
Hear=Setup - HomerView dialog
Hear=Welcome to the HomerView Setup Wizard
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Enter takes Next on each page; the defaults are right.
Key=Enter
Hear=Select Destination Location
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The last page offers the scripts for each screen reader it finds on this computer, ticked, each saying Install, Update or Reinstall. For one reader it also compiles the scripts for every version installed and asks the reader to reload them, so no restart is normally needed.
Key=Tab
Hear=(the box for your screen reader's scripts, its first word, checked)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A planned misstep: clearing that box. HomerView's keys would then do nothing. Space ticks it back.
Key=Space
Hear=checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Enter installs.
Key=Enter
Hear=Finish button
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The key on HomerView's desktop icon opens it from anywhere, with any screen reader or none.
Key=Alt+Control+Shift+H
Hear=HomerView
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=To confirm which build is loaded: the hotkey summary's first line.
Key=Alt+Shift+H
Hear=(the version, and when it was installed)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=If the opening key does nothing, another program has taken it; set a different one in the icon's properties. What this walk taught. I name the step; the reader gives the key.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Open HomerView.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Control plus Shift plus H

[step]

Say=The documentation is a key away from any page. Control plus F1 opens the user guide in the HomerView window; plain F1 stays Edge's own help.
Key=Control+F1
Hear=HomerView User Guide
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus F1 opens the quick start, the first ten minutes of HomerView, for anyone new to it.
Key=Alt+Shift+F1
Hear=HomerView Quick Start
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Shift plus F1 opens the history of changes, and Alt plus F1 says the version and where HomerView keeps its files.
Key=Alt+F1
Hear=About HomerView
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus H, Hotkey Summary, lists every command with its key in a window of its own, the quickest way to learn the keys.
Key=Alt+Shift+H
Hear=Hotkey Summary
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus F10, the Alternate Menu, lists every command in one alphabetized list, for the moment a key will not come to mind.
Key=Alt+F10
Hear=Alternate Menu
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape closes it without running anything.
Key=Escape
Hear=HomerView
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus F11 checks for a newer HomerView and installs it, as F11 does in other Homer programs.
Key=

[step]

Say=If something goes wrong, Alt plus Shift plus L copies the log to the clipboard as a file, ready to attach to an email.
Key=

[step]

Say=HomerView keeps its own copy of the browser, so its settings and its sign ins never disturb your everyday Edge.
Key=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus B, Choose Browser, picks which Chromium browser it drives, from those installed here.
Key=Alt+Shift+B
Hear=Choose Browser dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape leaves the choice as it was.
Key=Escape
Hear=HomerView
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Which build is loaded.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Shift plus H
